                help    "Krylov method AMGCL wraps around its multigrid preconditioner. cg (conjugate gradient) is the standard choice for the symmetric positive-definite systems Newton produces; bicgstab, gmres and their variants also handle nonsymmetric systems at a higher memory cost. AMGCL only exists in binaries built with it; other builds log a warning and fall back to the default solver."
